# The Theorist, Jace Beleren's -6 counts X after the draw: with no cards in the library nothing is drawn (CR 121.4), and with an
# empty hand X is 0, so no counters are put on the Illusions ("zero counters" is nothing, CR 107.1b). Bot1's deck is exactly the
# 13 cards its game draws: Jace draws on Bot2's turns 2, 4 and 6, and turns 3 and 5 draw; Bot2 empties Bot1's hand on turn 6
# with Mind Twist for 7 (Black Lotus, three Swamps and two Moxen), and on turn 7 Bot1 draws its last card, plays it and uses the -6
# (Jace at 6 after three +1s) with nothing in hand or library. The three Illusions have no counters, and Bot1 then loses for
# having drawn from an empty library (CR 704.5b).

